{"content":[{"c":["HEMAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Lotan’s son, the brother of Hori and a descendant of Seir the Horite (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.22","r":"Gen.36.22","rawR":"Gen.36.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.22","value":"Gen.36.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:22"},"); alternately spelled Homam in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.39","r":"1Chr.1.39","rawR":"1Chr.1.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.39","value":"1Chr.1.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 1:39"},", reflecting a later scribal error."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Mahol’s son, descendant of Zerah from Judah’s tribe and one of the sages whose wisdom was surpassed by King Solomon’s (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.31","r":"1Kgs.4.31","rawR":"1Kgs.4.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.31","value":"1Kgs.4.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.6","r":"1Chr.2.6","rawR":"1Chr.2.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.6","value":"1Chr.2.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:6"},"). He is perhaps the Ezrahite and author of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.1-18","r":"Ps.88.1-18","rawR":"Ps.88.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.1-18","value":"Ps.88.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 88"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Kohathite Levite, Joel’s son and one appointed, along with Asaph and Ethan (also called Jeduthun), by David to lead the musicians in the sanctuary (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.33","r":"1Chr.6.33","rawR":"1Chr.6.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.33","value":"1Chr.6.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","r":"1Chr.15.17","rawR":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.17","value":"1Chr.15.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.41","r":"1Chr.16.41","rawR":"1Chr.16.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.41","value":"1Chr.16.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:41"},"). During the transport of the ark from Obed-edom’s house to Jerusalem, he was responsible for sounding the bronze cymbals (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.19","r":"1Chr.15.19","rawR":"1Chr.15.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.19","value":"1Chr.15.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.12","r":"2Chr.5.12","rawR":"2Chr.5.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.12","value":"2Chr.5.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 5:12"},"). Heman fathered 14 sons and 3 daughters, all of whom served as musicians in the Lord’s house (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1-6","r":"1Chr.25.1-6","rawR":"1Chr.25.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1-6","value":"1Chr.25.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 25:1-6"},"). Later, his descendants participated in the cleansing of the temple during King Hezekiah’s reign (715–686 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.14","r":"2Chr.29.14","rawR":"2Chr.29.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.14","value":"2Chr.29.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:14"},") and assisted with the Passover celebration initiated by King Josiah (640–609 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.15","r":"2Chr.35.15","rawR":"2Chr.35.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.15","value":"2Chr.35.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Heman","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 36:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.22","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.22","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 1:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.39","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.39","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.39"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.31","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.31","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.6"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 88","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.88.1-18","rawQueryValue":"Ps.88.1-18","sourceRefExact":"Ps.88.1-18"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.33","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.33","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.33"},{"anchorText":"15:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.17"},{"anchorText":"16:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.41"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.19"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 5:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.5.12","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.5.12","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.5.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 25:1-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.25.1-6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.25.1-6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.25.1-6"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 35:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.35.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.35.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.35.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c55bf4b7ea1a006c45a7af6fbd575213879bb922cbb52d3659ab00bf883b89ec","sourceItemName":"Heman","sourceItemOrder":240,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Heman","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Heman","title":"Heman","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3